===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any [[plant]] whose [[foliage]] is covered with [[sting]]ing, mildly poisonous hairs, causing an instant rash.
## Especially, most species of herb genus ''[[Urtica]]'', the [[stinging nettle]]s:
### Most, but not all, subspecies of ''[[Urtica dioica]]'' ({{vern|common nettle}}),
### {{taxlink|Urtica incisa|species}} ({{vern|Australian nettle}});
## [[wood nettle|Wood nettle]] ({{taxlink|Laportea canadensis|species}});
## {{vern|bull nettle|Bull nettle}}s and {{vern|spurge nettle}}s (''[[Cnidoscolus]]'' spp.):
### {{taxlink|Cnidoscolus stimulosus|species}}, {{vern|bull nettle}}, {{vern|spurge nettle}},
### {{taxlink|Cnidoscolus texanus|species}}, {{vern|Texas bull nettle}},
### {{taxlink|Cnidoscolus urens|species}}, {{vern|bull nettle}},
### [[nettle tree|Nettle trees]] or {{vern|tree nettle}}s:
#### Various species of the genus {{taxlink|Dendrocnide|genus}}:
#### {{taxlink|Urera baccifera|species}} ([[scratchbush]]),
#### {{taxlink|Urtica ferox|species}} ({{vern|tree nettle}});
## {{vern|rock nettle}} ({{taxlink|Eucnide|genus}} spp.);
## {{vern|small-leaved nettle}} ({{taxlink|Dendrocnide photinophylla|species}}).
# Certain plants that have spines or prickles:
## {{vern|ball nettle}} ({{taxlink|Solanum carolinense|species}});
## {{taxlink|Solanum elaeagnifolium|species}}, {{vern|bull nettle}}, {{vern|silver-leaf nettle}}, {{vern|white horse-nettle}};
## {{taxlink|Solanum dimidiatum|species}}, {{vern|western horse-nettle}}, {{vern|robust horse-nettle}};
## {{taxlink|Solanum rostratum|species}}, {{vern|horse-nettle}};
## ''[[Celtis]]'' ([[hackberry]]).
# Certain non-stinging plants, mostly in the family [[Lamiaceae]], that resemble the species of ''Urtica'':
## {{vern|dead nettle}}, {{vern|dumb nettle}} (''[[Lamium]]'' spp.), particularly {{taxlink|Lamium album|species}}, {{vern|white nettle}};
## {{vern|false nettle}} ({{taxlink|Boehmeria|genus}} spp., family [[Urticaceae]]);
## {{vern|flame nettle}} or {{vern|painted nettle}} (''[[Coleus]]'' spp.);
## {{vern|hedge nettle}} (''[[Stachys]]'' spp.);
## [[vern|hemp nettle]] (''[[Galeopsis]]'' spp.);
## [[horse nettle]] {{taxlink|Agastache urticifolia|species}},
## {{vern|nilgiri nettle}}, {{vern|Himalayan giant nettle}} ({{taxlink|Girardinia diversifolia|species}}, family [[Urticaceae]]).
# Loosely, anything which causes a similarly stinging rash, such as a [[jellyfish]] or [[sea nettle]].

