===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} Of the nettle plant and similar physical causes, to sting, causing a rash in someone.
#:{{ux|en|The children were badly '''nettled''' after playing in the field.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 4-1|act=I|scene=iii|passage={{...}} I am whipp’d and scourged with rods, / '''Nettled''' and stung with pismires, when I hear / Of this vile politician, Bolingbroke.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figurative}} To [[pique]], [[irritate]], [[vex]] or [[provoke]].
#* {{RQ:Browne Hydriotaphia|pages=110–111|pageref=111|passage=[T]his is no lavv unto the vvoof of the neat ''Retiarie'' Spider, vvhich ſeems to vveave vvithout tranſverſion, and by the union of right lines to make out a continued ſurface, vvhich is beyond the common art of Textury, and may ſtill '''nettle''' ''{{w|Minerva}}'' the Godeſſe of that myſtery.}}
#* {{RQ:Behn Feign'd Curtizans|page=59|passage=His Miſtreſs: vvhoſe Miſtreſs, vvhat Miſtreſs; s'life hovv that little vvord has '''nettled''' me!}}
#* {{RQ:Richardson Pamela|volume=I|letter=XXXI|passage=I saw Mr. ''Williams'' was a little '''nettled''' at my Impatience {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1985|author=United States|publisher=Foreign Broadcast Information Service|journal=Daily Report: People's Republic of China|issue=180-189|page=42|passage=Liu, whose political writings had '''nettled''' the Taiwanese authorities, was assassinated on October 15, last year, in Daly City {{...}}}}

